[8th June 2026]

Okay cubic is opened, I set everything up and now I am in the terminal root.

Okay now its time to install plank and conky using

apt update
apt install plank conky-all -y

And then I made a folder: mkdir -p /root_assets
And then I unzipped origin files: tar -xzvf origin-os.tar.gz -C /root_assets

Install Themes and Icons System-Wide:
To ensure the login screen and all applications can see your MacOS themes and cursors, they belong in the /usr/share directories.

cp -r /root_assets/.icons/* /usr/share/icons/
cp -r /root_assets/.themes/* /usr/share/themes/


Set Up the Default User Experience (/etc/skel):
Now, we move your personal configurations into the skeleton directory so every new installation inherits them.

mkdir -p /etc/skel/.config
mkdir -p /etc/skel/.local/share

cp -r /root_assets/.config/conky /etc/skel/.config/
cp -r /root_assets/.local/share/plank /etc/skel/.local/share/
cp -r /root_assets/.config/autostart /etc/skel/.config/
cp -r /root_assets/.config/dconf /etc/skel/.config/


Cleanup:
rm -rf /root_assets origin_assets.zip
apt autoremove -y
apt clean

